Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: fix PWM backlight millipercent conversion

Commit 3c108046e1d6 ("drm/amd/display: Add power module on Linux")
switched the non-AUX (PWM) backlight path from writing the 16-bit PWM
level directly with dc_link_set_backlight_level() to passing a
millipercent value to mod_power_set_backlight_percent():

	brightness = DIV_ROUND_CLOSEST(brightness * 100, (max - min)) * 1000;

By this point convert_brightness_from_user() has already mapped the
user's value into the absolute range [min, max], where min and max come
from get_brightness_range() (0x101 * the ACPI ATIF min/max_input_signal).
mod_power_set_backlight_percent() however expects a value relative to
that range, because backlight_millipercent_to_pwm() computes:

	pwm = min_backlight_pwm +
	      millipercent * backlight_range / 100000;

The conversion is therefore wrong in three ways:

 - min is never subtracted, so the bottom of the range is unreachable:
   the dimmest setting requests min * 100000 / (max - min) millipercent
   instead of 0.

 - the quotient is computed in whole percent and only then multiplied by
   1000, so the usable resolution collapses to 100 steps regardless of
   the advertised max_brightness.

 - the result can exceed 100000, so the top of the user range is clamped
   and becomes a dead zone.

On an AYANEO SLIDE, where ATIF reports min_input_signal 38 and
max_input_signal 218 (so min = 9766, max = 56026 and max_brightness is
56026), the observable effects are:

 - brightness 0 requests 21000 millipercent instead of 0, so the panel
   cannot be dimmed below roughly 21% of its range
 - the backlight level only changes every ~560 of the 56026 steps
 - every value above ~43915 of 56026 is clamped to 100%

Convert to millipercent relative to [min, max], and scale before
dividing so the full precision is retained.

Fixes: 3c108046e1d6 ("drm/amd/display: Add power module on Linux")
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
@@ -5448,13 +5448,14 @@
 	if (caps->aux_support) {
 		rc = mod_power_set_backlight_nits(dm->power_module, stream, brightness,
 			AUX_BL_DEFAULT_TRANSITION_TIME_MS, false, true);
 	} else {
 		/* power module uses millipercent */
 		get_brightness_range(caps, &min, &max);
-		brightness = DIV_ROUND_CLOSEST(brightness * 100, (max - min)) * 1000;
+		brightness = DIV_ROUND_CLOSEST_ULL((u64)(brightness - min) * 100000,
+						   max - min);
 		rc = mod_power_set_backlight_percent(dm->power_module, stream,
 						     brightness, 0, false);
 	}
 
 	/*
 	 * Some kms clients create a ramped backlight transition effect
